{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571381417,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI5NDk1MTI1Nw=="},"target":"f5e8ba6de77254ccca9096c45871094484a445736efc450937aec4827823452f","message":"Issues happens whenever a submodule is placed into a 2nd-level subdirectory. The culprit is that `git submodule add` itself does not validate paths and converts them into POSIX form. One ends up with:\n\n```\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\datalad_temp_g1ojzium\u003ecat .gitmodules\n[submodule \"subdir/subds\"]\n        path = subdir\\\\subds\n        url = ./subdir/subds\n        datalad-id = 0f1a6694-f172-11e9-8ae6-309c23c2cf5c\n```\n\non which Git cannot act anymore:\n\n```\nFailed to run ['git', 'submodule', 'update', '--checkout', '--init', '--', 'subdir\\\\subds'] under 'C:\\\\Users\\\\mih\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\datalad_temp_bvprm457'. Exit code=128. out= err=fatal: No url found for submodule path 'subdir/subds' in .gitmodules\n```\n\nThe solution is to ensure that paths are specified in or converted to POSIX form.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571381402,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3MjM3MjY3MTI="},"added":["windows"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571381402,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3MjM3MjY3MTM="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571382014,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MjcyMzc0OTg0OQ=="},"title":"GitRepo.add_submodule(subdir/subdir) broken on Windows","was":"GitRepo.add_submodule(subdir/subdir) broken on Windows"},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571388288,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjcyNDA0MjYyMA=="},"status":2}]}